# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in, or leave the file out entirely.
#
# Everything here is public. Nothing in this app is a secret, because
# `output: "export"` means there is no server to keep one in: these values are
# readable by anyone who opens the page and none of them authorises anything on
# its own.
#
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is what makes a value reach the browser under Next, and a static
# export bakes it in at build time, so changing any of these means a rebuild.


# THE CHAIN

# Which network this build runs against. One of `robinhood-testnet` or
# `robinhood-mainnet`, the keys in `src/config/networks.ts`.
#
# Left unset it is testnet, and the asymmetry is deliberate: a build that forgot
# to name a network runs against the chain where a mistake costs nothing, and
# reaching mainnet takes somebody typing its name.
#
# A name this build does not know fails `npm run build` rather than falling back
# to the default. A typo that quietly landed on testnet in a build meant for
# mainnet would read an empty pool, and an empty pool looks exactly like an
# account with no money in it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COWL_NETWORK=robinhood-testnet


# SIGN IN

# Without the app id below the app still runs and every screen behind the door
# is still reachable with `SKIP_LOGIN` in `src/config/ui.ts`. What you lose is
# the Google button, which reports that this build has no credentials rather
# than failing at the provider's door with a page nobody can read.
#
# Both ids are public identifiers and neither authorises anything on its own:
# Privy checks the request origin against an allowlist held in its dashboard.
# The app secret that CAN act on an account is not here and must never be ·
# it lives on a laptop and is read only by `npm run probe:privy`.

# Privy · Dashboard · App settings · App ID.
# In that same dashboard: allowlist this app's origin, enable Google, and turn
# OFF every other login method. A second method is a second door into the same
# shielded account, and the weakest one sets the strength of all of them.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# Privy · Dashboard · App settings · Clients · Client ID. Optional.
# One app can serve several clients and the origin allowlist is held per client,
# so naming the client is what lets an origin be pinned to this build.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional. Where the provider returns the browser after Google. Left blank the
# SDK returns to the page that started the flow, which is right for a laptop and
# for any deployment served from the host being visited. Set it when a build is
# served from a host it cannot read off `window.location`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_REDIRECT_URL=
